- linux
verilator --binary --trace -Wall --timing -Wno-fatal CPU_tb.sv top.sv && ./obj_dir/VCPU_tb && python3 strip_top.py wave.vcd && gtkwave wave.vcd cpu_sim.gtkw

- mac
verilator --binary --trace -Wall --timing -Wno-fatal CPU_tb.sv top.sv && ./obj_dir/VCPU_tb && python3 strip_top.py wave.vcd && surfer wave.vcd cpu_sim.gtkw

Notes:
* strip_top.py removes Verilator's synthetic `TOP` wrapper scope from the VCD.
  Without it signals are TOP.CPU_tb.top_inst.*, cpu_sim.gtkw expects
  CPU_tb.top_inst.*, and GTKWave silently shows an empty signal pane.
  It is idempotent, so re-running it is harmless.
* --trace always emits VCD regardless of the $dumpfile name. Renaming the
  output to .fst does NOT make it FST; GTKWave picks its loader by extension
  and reports "could not initialize". Real FST needs --trace-fst, which needs
  `sudo apt install zlib1g-dev` (Verilator's FST writer links zlib).
* `make -C obj_dir -f VCPU_tb.mk` is unnecessary; --binary already builds.
